  "cover_text": "In a small bowl, combine fennel, capers, rosemary, orange zest, lime peel, and a pinch of salt. Add cucumber. Season with pepper. Refrigerate, until ready to serve.\nPrepare thinly sliced cheese slices. Sprinkle lettuce with cheese. Serve ice-cold. (Note: Hard cheese only serves on the spicy side, and hard cheese costs more and tends to break down more quickly than softer cheeses.)\nFrom Jennette: \"Makes 14 large thick slices, 2-3 medium sopes. (1 slice was rare..yet perfect when you butchered it with a cheddar and fresh fennel and + some chives). To freeze in ice cube trays, pour cheese to filling and freeze. The consumption of this",
